 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Keep simple. A few short speeches, a few plants, and some good food. A minute of silence is powerful on its own. The couple getting married themselves is the best. They can share what they've built together. A close friend or family member can back them up too. Yes. A candle lighting ritual works well. Each guest gets a candle, and you pass them out as the couple walks down the aisle. Perfect. A small potted tree or shrub that blooms in summer would be lovely.",
